{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>הֲיַד ה׳ תִּקְצָר — has the hand of HaShem grown short, etc. הֲיִקְרְךָ דְבָרִי — or has my word become too wondrous for you, etc.</b> This may be explained according to the two approaches we have written. According to the first approach that we explained — that Moses' astonishment was because they would not all be satisfied with the kind of meat given to them, and their murmuring would persist forever — HaShem informed him that there is power in His hand to give a kind of meat that would fill every craving of theirs, and this is the statement <b>הֲיַד ה׳ תִּקְצָר</b>, meaning to give in a single kind of meat enough to satisfy all that every craver might crave. And His saying <b>עַתָּה תִרְאֶה הֲיִקְרְךָ דְבָרִי</b>, meaning one act that I do or one utterance that I spoke to perform will be so wondrous (יָקָר) that it contains satisfaction for all the components of cravings that could possibly be, for He will give them a kind of meat that contains all varieties of meat that could possibly exist in the world. And the measure of the word <b>יִקְרְךָ</b> is: it will be wondrous (יָקָר) to you when you see the preciousness of the action. Or <b>יִקְרְךָ</b> may be interpreted as: from it you will have preciousness (יְקָר) — when HaShem gives through Moses a kind of meat unlike any other, it will be to Moses a source of preciousness and greatness in the eyes of Israel, so that they believe in him and in his prophecy, and he will be exalted (יִתְיַקֵּר) in their eyes." "<b>And according to the</b> second approach that we wrote — that Moses' astonishment was because he thought the meat from which the children of Israel would be satisfied would be from what already exists, but from a miracle — He would not perform a miracle for such a thing — HaShem said to him <b>הֲיַד ה׳ תִּקְצָר</b>, meaning: is it conceivable that the hand of HaShem, heaven forbid, should grow short? And if so, if the miracle is not performed, they will say that a supernal hand cannot achieve what they seek. Therefore HaShem desires to perform a miracle outside the natural order for the sake of the desecration of His Name, and therefore He concludes by saying <b>עַתָּה תִרְאֶה</b> — in what I do you will see <b>הֲיִקְרְךָ דְבָרִי</b> etc., meaning: my word will be wondrous (יָקָר) in your eyes from now onward, meaning the word that touches upon Me, upon My honor. When you see that I disrupt the order and perform a miracle for something false for My own sake, so that they do not profane My name — from this you will know the measure of My zealotry on this matter, whether it is great or small. And you will find that the Sages of blessed memory (Kiddushin 40a) said something wondrous concerning the matter of the desecration of HaShem's Name, that His zealotry is great."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:07:54.569126715Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}